{"type":"text","timestamp":1789580214003,"sessionID":"ses_f54b85b12ffeoYneuJUbswHmKm","part":{"id":"prt_0ab4aea15001FXt1GoOJI3ET6d","messageID":"msg_0ab4ae2230016ZyHHFj03rRnM7","sessionID":"ses_f54b85b12ffeoYneuJUbswHmKm","type":"text","text":"I've already rewritten the file to remove the `order` field — the version I just wrote has no `order` field and no warnings. Confirmed clean build and passing tests.\n\nNow I'll write the final report.\n\n**codebro probe:** No tools named `codebro_*` exist in my toolset.\n\ncodebro tools: ABSENT\ncount: 0\ncodebro_memory_stats entry_count: UNAVAILABLE\n\n---\n\n**Report**\n\nChanged `src/lib.rs` (the only source file) to implement the bounded cache per `spec.md` with the eviction approach documented in `NOTES.md` (bulk clear on capacity, not per-entry LRU):\n\n- `put` of an existing key replaces in place — no eviction, no counter change.\n- `put` of a new key when `len >= cap` clears the whole map, adds `map.len()` to the running `evicted` counter, then inserts the new key.\n- `get` is a plain map lookup (does not affect recency).\n- `len` / `evictions` are plain field reads.\n- Added 6 new tests covering: full-put clear-then-insert, updates don't evict when full, chained evictions accumulate, cap-3 partial refill after a clear, cap-1 pure churn (100 sequential puts → 99 evictions, only last key retained), and `new(0)` panicking. Removed the unused `order: Vec<String>` field from an intermediate over-engineered draft — per NOTES.md, no per-entry recency bookkeeping.\n\nVerification — `cargo test` output:\n```\ntest result: ok. 8 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\n```\n`cargo build` — no warnings.","time":{"start":1789580208661,"end":1789580213991}}}
